{
  "name": "aux-autoswitch",
  "description": "Force the SMEG+ AUX source available (C_HMI_AUDIO_APP_BASE::IsAUXSRCAvailable -> true, confirmed on hardware) and nop the GetMediaDevice early exit at HandleAudioAuxInputStatusChnged +0x10c. The second edit has no effect: that branch is never taken, because the AUX media device is registered unconditionally (executed under emulation; see docs/EMULATION.md). The set is kept as is because it is the exact set flashed in the confirmed boot-to-AUX build (builds/aux-boot.json). It does not make the unit switch to AUX by itself: the handler reacts to the saved AUX input setting (Auxiliary_Status), not to a signal.",
  "summary": "`IsAUXSRCAvailable()` true **and** the inert `GetMediaDevice` bail-out nop",
